# Thin-VKG structural slice fixture for the Hybrid end-to-end integration test.
#
# This is a standalone .ttl slice modelled on the inline `_SLICE_TTL` fixture in
# tests/unit/test_hybrid_graph.py, but loaded from disk by the integration test's
# fetch stub. It holds ONLY the two kinds of triples the query-time verify path
# reads:
#
#   <classIRI>    vkg:mapsToTable  "table"          (built into class_by_table)
#   <predicate>   rdfs:domain      <classIRI>        (drives the qualified check)
#   <predicate>   vkg:mapsToColumn "table.column"    (built into pred_by_column)
#
# Two classes (Address, Party) and one predicate (hasStateTc) whose rdfs:domain
# is Address but which is mapped to a column on BOTH tables:
#
#   * address.state_tc — correctly domained (subject class Address is admitted
#     by the predicate's Address domain) -> grounds cleanly.
#   * party.state_tc   — WRONG class (subject class Party is NOT admitted by the
#     Address domain) -> a `property:<hasStateTc> on <Party>` qualified miss.
#
# The vocab prefix (https://x#) matches the `mapsTo*` predicate IRIs below and is
# what the test passes as HybridDeps.vocab.
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix vkg: <https://x#> .

<http://x/Address> vkg:mapsToTable "address" .
<http://x/Party>   vkg:mapsToTable "party" .

<http://x/hasStateTc> rdfs:domain <http://x/Address> .
<http://x/hasStateTc> vkg:mapsToColumn "address.state_tc" .
<http://x/hasStateTc> vkg:mapsToColumn "party.state_tc" .
